        "id": 19233,
        "name": "bolnerap",
        "username": "bolnerap",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bolnerap/{size}/6056_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-04T02:07:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Challenge Omnitron vs. Setting Sun Ra, Freedom Five Absolute Zero, and Xtreme Prime Wardens Tempest.</p>\n<p>Mint with Ra at 20, AZ at 1 (where he hung out for several consecutive rounds), and Tempest at 8. The Challenge rules never came into play for me; I only saw two Components, and they came out one at a time, by which time Ra was set up to do 6-10 damage per round easily depending on whether Adaptive Plating was out or not. Unfortunately, I saw a lot of healing drones (almost every recycled \"drone or component\" was a healing drone), which extended the game more than I would have liked. Once I finally saw Obsidian Field, we burst him down quickly, with the only question being \"would I be able to save Absolute Zero\".</p>\n<p>There was way too much equipment destruction flying around for AZ to stay set up, sadly. Ra just laughed and kept healing. Never used Ra's base power.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:50.944Z",
