      {
        "id": 227731,
        "name": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "username": "starkenburg_alexander",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/starkenburg_alexander/{size}/1857_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-04T15:12:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint on a rollercoaster ride of HP. I don't remember where everyone ended up, but at one point all 3 were around 3, and later AZ was back to full, then back to 2, then 20 again....<br>\n<br>\nAnyway, only real problem I had was Electro-Pulse with three heroes is kind of hard to manage, especially since Tempest's power only affects the End of Turn effects, not Start of Turn. Though I do wonder if Sub-Zero Atmosphere with Thunderstruck would actually work... Has someone tried that?<br>\n<br>\nSedative Flechettes are annoying, Singularities are annoying, blah blah blah, the usual Omnitron stuff. Slowing him down with Into the Stratosphere did seem to help. Environment was more harm than help until I got to the Obsidian Fields, at which point the heroes wailed him down pretty good.<br>\n<br>\n~Komori</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:01:59.558Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
